# Build Then Push

After finishing code changes for this repo:

1. Run `yarn build` and fix any build failures until green.
2. Commit relevant changes (never secrets).
3. Push to `origin main` only after the build succeeds.
4. Do not push if the production build fails.

Use yarn for scripts. Prefer this flow even when the user only says "push" after recent fixes — verify build first, then push.
